Subject: [PATCH] Render seasonal backgrounds in the main menu

The seasonal background is checked ahead of the dynamic-background branch
because it is an explicit user opt-in, and it falls through to the existing
behaviour whenever getImage() returns null (option off, folder empty, or the
last decode failed).

This patch is deliberately additive: it inserts a new branch that ends with a
bare "} else" and leaves the existing dynamic-background "if" line in place as
following code, which Java reads as an else-if chain. Nothing is deleted, so
the hunk only has to match the unique parallaxY line and its closing brace.

The image is aspect-filled rather than scaled to fit, so arbitrary user image
sizes never stretch or letterbox. Parallax and the existing bgAlpha fade are
both preserved.

The per-frame getScaledCopy() mirrors what the MENU_BG path already does. It
is cheap because the copy shares the parent's TextureRegion, and it is never
destroyed: Image.destroy() cascades to parentImage, so destroying a scaled
copy would free the underlying texture out from under the loader.

Rerolls happen on menu entry and on track change, and leave() releases the
texture since the main menu is its only consumer.
---
 a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/MainMenu.java | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/MainMenu.java b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/MainMenu.java
--- a/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/MainMenu.java
+++ b/src/itdelatrisu/opsu/states/MainMenu.java
@@ -42,3 +42,4 @@
 import itdelatrisu.opsu.ui.NotificationManager.NotificationListener;
+import itdelatrisu.opsu.ui.SeasonalBackground;
 import itdelatrisu.opsu.ui.StarFountain;
 import itdelatrisu.opsu.ui.UI;
@@ -349,2 +350,17 @@
 			parallaxY = -offset / 2f * (mouseY - height / 2) / (height / 2);
 		}
+		// Seasonal backgrounds take priority: they are an explicit user choice.
+		// Falls through to the existing behaviour when getImage() returns null
+		// (option off, folder empty, or the last decode failed).
+		Image seasonalBg = SeasonalBackground.getImage();
+		if (seasonalBg != null) {
+			// Aspect-fill so arbitrary user image sizes never stretch.
+			float coverScale = Math.max(
+				(float) width / seasonalBg.getWidth(),
+				(float) height / seasonalBg.getHeight());
+			if (Options.isParallaxEnabled())
+				coverScale *= GameImage.PARALLAX_SCALE;
+			Image scaled = seasonalBg.getScaledCopy(coverScale);
+			scaled.setAlpha(bgAlpha.getValue());
+			scaled.drawCentered(width / 2 + parallaxX, height / 2 + parallaxY);
+		} else
@@ -692,3 +708,7 @@
 		// reset measure info
 		lastMeasureProgress = 0f;
 		starFountain.clear();
+
+		// Pick a fresh seasonal background each time the menu is entered.
+		SeasonalBackground.invalidate();
+		SeasonalBackground.reroll();
@@ -734,5 +754,8 @@
 		if (MusicController.isTrackDimmed())
 			MusicController.toggleTrackDimmed(1f);
+
+		// The menu is the only consumer; release GPU memory before gameplay.
+		SeasonalBackground.unload();
 
 		// reset overlays
 		optionsOverlay.deactivate();
@@ -1009,4 +1032,8 @@
 		if (Options.isDynamicBackgroundEnabled() && !sameAudio && !MusicController.isThemePlaying())
 			bgAlpha.setTime(0);
+		if (Options.isSeasonalBackgroundEnabled()) {
+			SeasonalBackground.reroll();
+			bgAlpha.setTime(0);
+		}
 		musicInfoProgress.setTime(0);
 	}
@@ -1022,4 +1049,8 @@
 			if (Options.isDynamicBackgroundEnabled())
 				bgAlpha.setTime(0);
+			if (Options.isSeasonalBackgroundEnabled()) {
+				SeasonalBackground.reroll();
+				bgAlpha.setTime(0);
+			}
 		}
 		musicInfoProgress.setTime(0);
